  "body": "### Summary\nAfter a device test (2026-11-07), the operator reports that lists and the reader lack visual separation and consistency, and asks to align them with the MP list, Settings and Apple's Notes app. This umbrella keeps one definition instead of case-by-case fixes. Milestone **M4**: per the operator, nothing they report goes to M5.\n\n### Issues under this umbrella\n- #568: reader message separation (alternating tint and a stronger separator).\n- #570: unread MP row tint, through a shared `RowTint` helper that the super-favourite row also uses.\n- #569: MP avatar (cache fill and monogram).\n- #427: the Catégories list, which uses `.sidebar` today. Its rebuild takes the explicit inset-grouped style (comment on #427).\n\n### Definition (to record as a GAP row or a note in `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, not a new document)\n**Native lists**: Catégories, topic lists, favourites, MPs, search, filtered posts, offline, accounts, profile.\n- Use one explicit `List` style (inset-grouped), with system separators and system background colours.\n- Express state only through `RowTint`, and always with a dot or text cue as well.\n- Take insets, avatar size and density from `ListDensity` only.\n\n**Reader**: one token set (`--surface-alt`, `--separator-strong`, `--alt-strength`) derived from `--text` and `--background`, so light, dark, OLED, classic and the dark-brightness slider all inherit it.\n\n**Coordination**: LOT-122 (#213, separators and OLED), and #545 (glass bars and scroll edge).\n\n### Acceptance\n- The sub-issues are merged.\n- Every list uses an explicit style (`git grep listStyle` shows no implicit list left).\n- One Mac pass checks light, dark, Increase Contrast and Dynamic Type XL across all lists.",
